es-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Creates and shows or hides and destroys the on-sceen profiler ui\n\nThe profiler is a real-time tool that shows the numbers of milliseconds spent\nin each scope per frame as well as counters. The profiler is very useful for\ntracking down performance and resource problems.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Show the profiler UI\nprofiler.enable_ui(true)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.enable_ui:enabled)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.enable_ui","jsName":"enableUi","line":112,"member":"enable_ui","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"true to enable, false to disable","optional":false,"rawName":"enabled","rawType":"boolean"}],"rawName":"profiler.enable_ui","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Get the percent of CPU usage by the application, as reported by the OS.\n\nThis function is not available on  HTML5.\n\nFor some platforms ( Android,  Linux and  Windows), this information is only available\nby default in the debug version of the engine. It can be enabled in release version as well\nby checking `track_cpu` under `profiler` in the `game.project` file.\n(This means that the engine will sample the CPU usage in intervalls during execution even in release mode.)\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.get_cpu_usage:)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.get_cpu_usage","jsName":"getCpuUsage","line":125,"member":"get_cpu_usage","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[],"rawName":"profiler.get_cpu_usage","returnDescriptions":["percent of CPU used by the application"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Get the detailed amount of memory used by the application in bytes, as reported by the platform.\n\nThe values are gathered from internal OS functions which correspond to the following;\n\nOS                                | Value\n----------------------------------|------------------\niOS\n\nMacOS\n\nAndroid\n\nLinux | [Resident memory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resident_set_size)\nWindows            | [Working set](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Working_set)\nHTML5                | Allocated bytes reported by `mallinfo().uordblks`\n\n**Examples:**\n\nGet memory usage before and after loading a collection:\n\n```lua\nprint(profiler.get_memory_usage())\nmsg.post(\"#collectionproxy\", \"load\")\n...\nprint(profiler.get_memory_usage()) -- will report a higher number than the initial call\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.get_memory_usage:)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.get_memory_usage","jsName":"getMemoryUsage","line":156,"member":"get_memory_usage","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[],"rawName":"profiler.get_memory_usage","returnDescriptions":["bytes used by the application"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Send a text to the connected profiler\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprofiler.log_text(\"Event: \" .. name)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.log_text:text)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.log_text","jsName":"logText","line":168,"member":"log_text","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the string to send to the connected profiler","optional":false,"rawName":"text","rawType":"string"}],"rawName":"profiler.log_text","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Get the number of recorded frames in the on-screen profiler ui recording buffer\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Show the last recorded frame\nlocal recorded_frame_count = profiler.recorded_frame_count()\nprofiler.view_recorded_frame(recorded_frame_count)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.recorded_frame_count:)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.recorded_frame_count","jsName":"recordedFrameCount","line":182,"member":"recorded_frame_count","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[],"rawName":"profiler.recorded_frame_count","returnDescriptions":["frame_count the number of recorded frames, zero if on-screen profiler is disabled"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Starts a profile scope.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Go back one frame\nprofiler.scope_begin(\"test_function\")\n  test_function()\nprofiler.scope_end()\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.scope_begin:name)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.scope_begin","jsName":"scopeBegin","line":197,"member":"scope_begin","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"The name of the scope","optional":false,"rawName":"name","rawType":"string"}],"rawName":"profiler.scope_begin","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"End the current profile scope.\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.scope_end:)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.scope_end","jsName":"scopeEnd","line":202,"member":"scope_end","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[],"rawName":"profiler.scope_end","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Set the on-screen profile mode - run, pause, record or show peak frame\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nfunction start_recording()\n     profiler.set_ui_mode(profiler.MODE_RECORD)\nend\n\nfunction stop_recording()\n     profiler.set_ui_mode(profiler.MODE_PAUSE)\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.set_ui_mode:mode)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.set_ui_mode","jsName":"setUiMode","line":220,"member":"set_ui_mode","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the mode to set the ui profiler in  To stop recording, switch to a different mode such as `MODE_PAUSE` or `MODE_RUN`. You can also use the `view_recorded_frame` function to display a recorded frame. Doing so stops the recording as well.  Every time you switch to recording mode the recording buffer is cleared.","optional":false,"rawName":"mode","rawType":"profiler.MODE"}],"rawName":"profiler.set_ui_mode","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Set the on-screen profile view mode - minimized or expanded\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Minimize the profiler view\nprofiler.set_ui_view_mode(profiler.VIEW_MODE_MINIMIZED)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.set_ui_view_mode:mode)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.set_ui_view_mode","jsName":"setUiViewMode","line":233,"member":"set_ui_view_mode","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the view mode to set the ui profiler in","optional":false,"rawName":"mode","rawType":"profiler.VIEW_MODE"}],"rawName":"profiler.set_ui_view_mode","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Shows or hides the time the engine waits for vsync in the on-screen profiler\n\nEach frame the engine waits for vsync and depending on your vsync settings and how much time\nyour game logic takes this time can dwarf the time in the game logic making it hard to\nsee details in the on-screen profiler graph and lists.\n\nAlso, by hiding this the FPS times in the header show the time spent each time excuding the\ntime spent waiting for vsync. This shows you how long time your game is spending actively\nworking each frame.\n\nThis setting also effects the display of recorded frames but does not affect the actual\nrecorded frames so it is possible to toggle this on and off when viewing recorded frames.\n\nBy default the vsync wait times is displayed in the profiler.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Exclude frame wait time form the profiler ui\nprofiler.set_ui_vsync_wait_visible(false)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.set_ui_vsync_wait_visible:visible)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.set_ui_vsync_wait_visible","jsName":"setUiVsyncWaitVisible","line":259,"member":"set_ui_vsync_wait_visible","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"true to include it in the display, false to hide it.","optional":false,"rawName":"visible","rawType":"boolean"}],"rawName":"profiler.set_ui_vsync_wait_visible","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"Pauses and displays a frame from the recording buffer in the on-screen profiler ui\n\nThe frame to show can either be an absolute frame or a relative frame to the current frame.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Go back one frame\nprofiler.view_recorded_frame({distance = -1})\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.view_recorded_frame:frame_index)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:profiler.view_recorded_frame","jsName":"viewRecordedFrame","line":274,"member":"view_recorded_frame","modulePath":["profiler"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"a table where you specify one of the following parameters:  - `distance` The offset from the currently displayed frame (this is truncated between zero and the number of recorded frames) - `frame` The frame index in the recording buffer (1 is first recorded frame)","optional":false,"rawName":"frame_index","rawType":"{ distance:integer }|{ frame:integer }"}],"rawName":"profiler.view_recorded_frame","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/profiler.lua"}],"types":[{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","fields":[{"description":"Functions for getting profiling data in runtime.\nMore detailed [profiling](https://www.defold.com/manuals/profiling/) and [debugging](http://www.defold.com/manuals/debugging/) information available in the manuals.\npause on the currently displayed frame\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.MODE)","line":18,"optional":false,"rawName":"MODE_PAUSE","rawType":"profiler.MODE","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"record incoming frames to the recording buffer\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.MODE)","line":22,"optional":false,"rawName":"MODE_RECORD","rawType":"profiler.MODE","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"continuously show the latest frame\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.MODE)","line":26,"optional":false,"rawName":"MODE_RUN","rawType":"profiler.MODE","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"pause on the displayed frame, replacing it when a slower frame arrives\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.MODE)","line":30,"optional":false,"rawName":"MODE_SHOW_PEAK_FRAME","rawType":"profiler.MODE","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"show all profiler details\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/profiler-lua#profiler.VIEW_MODE)","line":34,"optional":false,"rawName":"VIEW_MODE_FULL","rawType":"profiler.VIEW_MODE","source":"doc/profiler.lua"},{"description":"show only the header with 